commit.message:
fix(google): preserve streamed tool ordering and signature history (#24349)

## Background

Google/Vertex streamed function calls were processed after other parts,
moving them behind later text. Empty signature-bearing parts also lost
their position or metadata when assistant history was reused.

## Summary

Process completed function calls in part order, separate surrounding
text/reasoning blocks, and preserve standalone thought signatures
through the stream, assistant history, and follow-up request. Core
retains empty text with non-null provider metadata. Existing
trailing-signature normalization and unfinished partial-argument
accumulation remain in place; completed partial-argument calls now
separate surrounding blocks; arbitrary unfinished partial-argument
interleaving and reconstruction of every original wire boundary remain
outside this fix.

Updated to main, added 16 regression cases for text/reasoning,
complete/no-args calls, both provider identities and within/across-chunk
parts. Moved the contributor's reproduction outside the checkout into
this body. Added patch changesets for all affected packages. Opus review
identified cross-provider empty-text compatibility and terminal
